      "**Hypothetical FastAPI documentation excerpt**\n\n> **What does `Depends` do?**  \n> `Depends` is a helper that tells FastAPI that a particular function parameter should be supplied by the framework rather than by the caller. When you declare a parameter as `param: SomeType = Depends(some_dependency)`, FastAPI will:\n> \n> 1. Call `some_dependency` (or any callable you provide) to obtain a value.  \n> 2. Resolve any dependencies that `some_dependency` itself declares, recursively.  \n> 3. Pass the resulting value into the parameter `param`.  \n> \n> This mechanism enables *dependency injection*: you can factor out common logic (e.g., database sessions, authentication checks, configuration values) into reusable callables and have FastAPI automatically provide them to your path operation functions, routers, or other dependencies."
